Our ministers take their oaths. The first act of the new cabinet is to open the police arsenals to the Hundreds. Berlin sends an ultimatum and the SPD ministers in the Reich government begin to wonder, in public, how long they will be asked to sit next to men who arm the workers of Saxony.

[? if comintern_trust < 50 : Moscow had not asked for this, and it is furious. The Executive reads the news as a party that has stopped listening, and says so in a telegram that is meant to be leaked. ?][? if comintern_trust >= 50 : Moscow, which has been consulted, approves. ?]

@refuse
subtitle: Moscow -3 trust, Left +5 dissent. · dev: trust −3, kf_left_dissent +5
on-arrival: comintern_trust -= 3; kf_left_dissent += 5
go-to: root

We keep our hands clean of the Land government. Zeigner is disappointed. The Left says that a Saxon cabinet that could have armed the workers has been wasted, and the Right says that it is better to wait.
